  "reviewedRulings": [
    "Use current membership and subject transaction locks plus database uniqueness for retry serialization; no additional cache or persistence framework.",
    "Five-minute preview TTL and 24-hour request tombstones describe operational cache retention, not personal-data or legal audit retention.",
    "Permission or subject-version changes invalidate snapshot access on read; cleanup is bounded and eventual. Proactive erasure-isolation hooks remain a later requirement."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Preparations always return executionAvailable=false; they never accept or authorize data deletion.",
    "Counts are a point-in-time snapshot, not an immutable deletion scope. Actual submission must revalidate all domains and persist an independent deletion ledger.",
    "Deletion execution, cross-domain isolation, external cleanup receipts, restore gating and management UI remain incomplete.",
    "Existing local services and business database were not replaced or reset.",
    "Full backend interoperability uses pre-existing isolated Dart/Flutter fixtures; no new frontend build or browser deletion journey is claimed.",
    "Native Android runner skip is not evidence of real-device enforcement.",
    "Full backend suite uses the recorded base plus preview changes; later committed commercial/identity changes received the separate targeted integration run. Foreign uncommitted work remains outside both candidates and the review."
  ]
